opper on that type of antenna are oxides. You can get, even microscopic, sections acting as diodes mixing signals out of the air with your own. Could you make a step diode that way?<br>\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XzHKaloTh6o\">YouTube</a></p>\n<div class=\"embed embed-youtube\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/XzHKaloTh6o\" title=\"YouTube\" allowfullscreen referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\"></iframe><p class=\"embed-fallback\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XzHKaloTh6o\">Watch on YouTube</a></p></div>","m":"<h1>Post 1707745232144536047</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1707745232144536047\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2023-09-29T13:12:46Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1707745658411618558":{"a":"<p>I made a playlist of related topics. If you&#x27;re into fiddling with radio and antennas but aren&#x27;t sure how things work:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLoGTHdPlE-US9YIhS5-GAn6me7TjIsG0G&amp;si=kRaP9dNhn2XEdg2G\">youtube.com/playlist?list=…</a></p>","m":"<h1>Post 1707745658411618558</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1707745658411618558\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2023-09-29T13:14:28Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1707760586396680477":{"a":"<p>t.co</p>\n<p><img class=\"media\" src=\"1707760586396680477-F7MvM5hWkAA9Mma.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p>","m":"<h1>Post 1707760586396680477</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1707760586396680477\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2023-09-29T14:13:47Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>zxx</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd>